# Django Security

- Never commit secrets. `SECRET_KEY`, DB passwords, and API tokens come from the environment.
- POST forms include `{% csrf_token %}`. HTMX requests must send the CSRF header.
- Use the ORM. Do not build SQL with f-strings or `%` interpolation.
- Validate at the boundary (forms, serializers). Do not trust hidden fields for `user_id`.
- `DEBUG` stays False in production. Do not log passwords or tokens.

See skills: `django-auth`, `django-rest-framework`.
